{"name": "Color Palettes K1", "id": "965f0cf5e389c936", "sources": {"main": "/* Color Palettes\n  Purpose \n  \n  In response to https://forum.electromage.com/t/color-palette-support/192\n  \n  FastLED allows you to specify a gradient palette in the form of a \n  series of four-number groups:\n    position, R, G, B,\n    position, R, G, B, ...etc\n  \n  Because many Pixelblaze patterns are built on hsv(), instead of rgb(), the \n  goal is to flexibly allow use of a palette to just specify hues, or to \n  specify any combination of hues, saturations, and values. \n  \n  The functions below allow you to either posterize (limit output to a few\n  discreet colors), or output a gradient that transitions smoothly between the\n  specified hues or colors (hue, saturation, and value).\n  \n  The question in interpolating a gradient should be, \"via what path?\".\n  \n  In a hue wheel, red and cyan are on opposite sides. These utilties allow you \n  to pick several paths, such as fading through white, black, green or yellow.\n\n  ============================ K1 INTEGRATION ============================\n  This copy adds:\n  1. The FULL K1 firmware palette bank (44 gradient palettes, generated\n     verbatim from SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/visual/Palettes.cpp, in\n     gGradientPalettes[] order). They render as modes 15..58 via an exact\n     RGB stop-walk (palSample) -- NOT converted to h/s/v remaps, because the\n     K1-native palettes are authored in gamma-corrected RGB output space with\n     deliberate dark separators that an 8-entry hue remap would destroy.\n  2. Smooth mode/palette transitions. The original pattern hard-cut the whole\n     strip once per second (mode = floor(numModes * time(...))). That is gone.\n     Every switch -- auto-cycle or manual -- now crossfades in RGB output\n     space: during a fade each pixel is evaluated under BOTH the outgoing and\n     incoming mode and mixed with a smoothstep ramp. Fade time and dwell time\n     are sliders; fade is clamped to 90% of dwell so an auto-cycle fade always\n     completes before the next switch begins.\n  UI:\n    ModeSelect   - manual palette/mode pick, 0..58 (0..14 = original HSV\n                   demos, 15..58 = K1 bank; 48..58 are the K1-native set)\n    AutoCycle    - toggle auto-advance (default on)\n    K1Only       - auto-cycle only the 44 K1 palettes, skip the HSV demos\n                   (default on; manual select always reaches everything)\n    DwellTime    - seconds each palette holds (1..30s)\n    FadeTime     - crossfade length (0.1..5s)\n  ========================================================================\n*/\n/* \n  Palette Arrays\n  \n  In Pixelblaze, the hue term allows us to pick colors without specifying the brightess\n  or 'whiteness' of a color, and wraps from 0...1 with red at both ends. A hue palette\n  remaps that 0-1 to a different 0-1 made of the colors we want to express. In addition\n  to hue, you can remap saturation and value (\"color grading\": grade(input, hsv_palette)).\n  \n  Palettes here are a sequence of colors at positions 0-999 (integer part) with the\n  0-0.999 decimal part as the value; entries must be sorted ascending by position.\n  See the original forum thread for the full walkthrough.\n  \n  hFn(input, palette)      - hue gradient, shortest path around the wheel\n  posterize(input, palette)- discreet lookup\n  unitFn(input, palette)   - linear remap without hue-wheel wrapping (for s, v)\n  grade(input, hsv_palette)- remap h, s and v together\n*/\n// Syntactic convenience. Load array elements, return the array.\nfunction set3(x0, x1, x2) {\n  arr = array(3)\n  arr[0] = x0; arr[1] = x1; arr[2] = x2;\n  return arr\n}\nfunction set8(x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7) {\n  arr = array(8)\n  arr[0] = x0; arr[1] = x1; arr[2] = x2; arr[3] = x3; arr[4] = x4; arr[5] = x5; arr[6] = x6; arr[7] = x7; \n  return arr\n}\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Crossfade output stage: modes no longer draw directly with hsv().\n// They write or/og/ob via outHsv() (HSV demos) or palSample() (K1 bank),\n// so render() can evaluate two modes and mix them during a transition.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------\nvar or, og, ob\nfunction outHsv(hh, ss, vv) {\n  hh = mod(hh, 1) * 6\n  var sec = floor(hh)\n  var f = hh - sec\n  var p = vv * (1 - ss), q = vv * (1 - ss * f), w = vv * (1 - ss * (1 - f))\n  if (sec == 0)      { or = vv; og = w;  ob = p }\n  else if (sec == 1) { or = q;  og = vv; ob = p }\n  else if (sec == 2) { or = p;  og = vv; ob = w }\n  else if (sec == 3) { or = p;  og = q;  ob = vv }\n  else if (sec == 4) { or = w;  og = p;  ob = vv }\n  else               { or = vv; og = q;  ob = p }\n}\n// Below are the 15 original demo palettes (unchanged apart from hsv -> outHsv).\nvar numHsvModes = 15\nvar modes = array(numHsvModes)\n// There's no array.length, so we define the expected size of all HSV-demo palettes.\nvar paletteSize = 8\n// No change; in-out linear-h rainbow. Notice posterize vs hFn.\nh0 = set8(0.0, 1.001, 50.050, 444.444, 555.555, 600.6, 900.9, 999.999)\nmodes[0] = (h, pct) => outHsv(posterize(h, h0), 1, 1)\nmodes[1] = (h, pct) => outHsv(hFn(h, h0), 1, 1)\n// A much better rainbow, similar to the \"perceptual hue utility\"\nh2 = set8(0.0, 111.015, 222.08, 333.3, 444.44, 555.65, 666.7, 888.985)\nmodes[2] = (h, pct) => outHsv(hFn(h, h2), 1, 1)\n// Blues & violets\nh3 = set8(0.66, 167.95, 333.85, 500.61, 725.61, 750.5, 800.5, 825.61)\ns3 = set8(0.999, 167.999, 333.8, 500.999, 725.999, 750.999, 800.999, 825.999)\nv3 = set8(0.2, 167.299, 333.299, 500.1, 725.1, 750.3, 800.3, 825.1)\nmodes[3] = (h, pct) => outHsv(posterize(h, h3), posterize(h, s3), posterize(h, v3))\nhsv_palette3 = set3(h3, s3, v3)\nmodes[4] = (h, pct) => grade(h, hsv_palette3)\n// Firey red-yellow \np5 = set8(0, 0.0, 0.0, 500.1, 555.0, 600.1, 666.0, 999.05)  // hue, fn of input hue\nv5 = set8(0.9, 100.9, 200.9, 300.1, 400.1, 500.01, 700.006, 999.0) // value, fn of position\nmodes[5] = (h, pct) => outHsv(hFn(h, p5), 1, unitFn(pct, v5))\n// Monochrome. This one really highlights for me how the color temperature of white\n//   is not at all constant over the 0-1 range of v (and global brightness setting)\nv6 = set8(0, 150.999, 151.0, 200.0, 201.999, 350.0, 900.999, 951.0) // value, fn of position\nmodes[6] = (h, pct) => {v = unitFn(h, v6); outHsv(0.05, 0.5, v * v)} // v stll looks best convex\n// Color wheel opposites; fade through white and black.\n// Red-white-cyan-black-purple-white-green-black-red\n// Notice no yellow, blue, magenta, orange present\np7 = set8(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 250.5, 500.75, 750.25)\ns7 = set8(0.999, 0.999, 200.999, 250.0, 300.999, 700.999, 750.0, 800.999) // fade through white\nv7 = set8(0, 0, 0, 50.999, 450.999, 500.0, 550.999, 950.999) // fade through black\nmodes[7] = (h, pct) => {\n  _h = posterize(h, p7)\n  s = unitFn(h, s7)\n  v = unitFn(h, v7)\n  outHsv(_h, s * s, v * v)\n}\n// The elusive search for Brown in RGB LEDs\nh8 = set8(0, 0, 0, 0, 400.04, 600.0, 800.07, 999.0)\ns8 = set8(0, 0, 0, 0.9999, 300.98, 500.9999, 800.94, 999.999)\nv8 = set8(0, 0, 0, 200.05, 400.0, 800.015, 900.05, 999.0)\nhsv_palette8 = set3(h8, s8, v8)\nmodes[8] = (h, pct) => grade(h, hsv_palette8)\n// Let's go pink to orange, kind of skipping red. Because I'm almost a millenial.\nh9 = set8(0, 0, 0, 0.94, 250.0133, 500.0100, 750.0133, 999.94)\ns9 = set8(0, 0, 0, 0.90, 250.9500, 500.9999, 750.9500, 999.90)\nmodes[9] = (h, pct) => outHsv(hFn(h, h9), unitFn(h, s9), 1)\n// Black, violet, pink, orange, yellow\nhsv_palette10 = set3(\n  set8(0.77, 143.83, 286.89, 429.95, 571.0, 714.02, 857.05, 999.06), // hue\n  set8(0.999, 143.999, 286.999, 429.999, 571.97, 714.999, 857.98, 999.97), // saturation\n  set8(0, 143.005, 286.01, 429.01, 571.1, 714.5, 857.5, 999.95) // value\n)\nmodes[10] = (h, pct) => grade(h, hsv_palette10)\n// Pink to purple through desat\nhsv_palette11 = set3(\n  set8(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0.99, 500.94, 999.78), // hue\n  set8(0, 0, 0, 0, 0.999, 300.9, 500.999, 999.97), // saturation\n  set8(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0.5, 500.005, 999.1) // value\n)\nmodes[11] = (h, pct) => grade(h, hsv_palette11)\n// Minty greens, transforming h before mapping saturation & value\nh12 = set8(0.39, 250.33, 251.45, 500.3, 501.33, 725.25, 726.3, 999.45)\ns12 = set8(0.5, 250.9, 251.999, 500.9, 501.9, 725.98, 726.95, 999.98)\nv12 = set8(0.003, 250.2, 251.5, 500.0, 501.04, 725.2, 726.005, 999.03)\nmodes[12] = (h, pct) => outHsv(\n  hFn(h, h12),\n  unitFn(h * 2 % 1, s12), \n  unitFn(1 - h, v12)\n)\n// Minty greens + minty pinks\nhsv_palette13 = set3(\n  set8(0.4, 125.3, 350.4, 351.95, 500.88, 625.99, 750.85, 990.94), // hue\n  set8(62.6, 187.0, 312.9, 437.8, 562.9, 677.9, 812.7, 937.9), // saturation\n  set8(62.1, 187.45, 312.2, 350.1, 562.9, 677.25, 912.7, 995.05) // value\n)\nmodes[13] = (h, pct) => grade(h, hsv_palette13)\n// Dawn\nhsv_palette14 = set3(\n  set8(0.0, 35.03, 400.04, 410.55, 900.67, 999.67, 999.67, 999.67), // hue\n  set8(0.8, 50.9, 400.3, 410.8, 500.8, 501.7, 725.7, 999.999), // saturation\n  set8(0.0, 35.3, 50.99, 500.5, 600.2, 999.0, 999.0, 999.0) // value\n)\nmodes[14] = (h, pct) => grade(h, hsv_palette14)\n// K1 palette bank -- generated verbatim from SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/visual/Palettes.cpp\n// Values are the FastLED gradient bytes /255 (already gamma-converted for WS2812B output).\n// Order matches the firmware gGradientPalettes[] bank (Palettes.h) exactly, all 44 entries.\nvar PAL_COUNT = 44\nvar palOff = [0, 7, 12, 16, 25, 27, 32, 37, 43, 49, 56, 64, 76, 85, 91, 98, 104, 112, 119, 123, 128, 134, 139, 143, 156, 163, 174, 181, 192, 205, 212, 217, 224, 229, 238, 249, 259, 268, 278, 288, 297, 307, 315, 324]\nvar palLen = [7, 5, 4, 9, 2, 5, 5, 6, 6, 7, 8, 12, 9, 6, 7, 6, 8, 7, 4, 5, 6, 5, 4, 13, 7, 11, 7, 11, 13, 7, 5, 7, 5, 9, 11, 10, 9, 10, 10, 9, 10, 8, 9, 6]\nvar palData = [\n  0, 0.4706, 0, 0, 0.0863, 0.702, 0.0863, 0, 0.2, 1, 0.4078, 0, 0.3333, 0.6549, 0.0863, 0.0706, 0.5294, 0.3922, 0, 0.4039, 0.7765, 0.0627, 0, 0.5098, 1, 0, 0, 0.6275,  // Sunset_Real\n  0, 0.0039, 0.0549, 0.0196, 0.3961, 0.0627, 0.1412, 0.0549, 0.6471, 0.2196, 0.2667, 0.1176, 0.949, 0.5882, 0.6118, 0.3882, 1, 0.5882, 0.6118, 0.3882,  // es_rivendell_15\n  0, 0.0039, 0.0235, 0.0275, 0.349, 0.0039, 0.3882, 0.4353, 0.6, 0.5647, 0.8196, 1, 1, 0, 0.2863, 0.3216,  // es_ocean_breeze_036\n  0, 0.0157, 0.0039, 0.1216, 0.1216, 0.2157, 0.0039, 0.0627, 0.2471, 0.7725, 0.0118, 0.0275, 0.3725, 0.2314, 0.0078, 0.0667, 0.498, 0.0235, 0.0078, 0.1333, 0.6235, 0.1529, 0.0235, 0.1294, 0.749, 0.4392, 0.051, 0.1255, 0.8745, 0.2196, 0.0353, 0.1373, 1, 0.0863, 0.0235, 0.149,  // rgi_15\n  0, 0.7373, 0.5294, 0.0039, 1, 0.1804, 0.0275, 0.0039,  // retro2_16\n  0, 0.0118, 0, 1, 0.2471, 0.0902, 0, 1, 0.498, 0.2627, 0, 1, 0.749, 0.5569, 0, 0.1765, 1, 1, 0, 0,  // Analogous_1\n  0, 0.4941, 0.0431, 1, 0.498, 0.7725, 0.0039, 0.0863, 0.6863, 0.8235, 0.6157, 0.6745, 0.8667, 0.6157, 0.0118, 0.4392, 1, 0.6157, 0.0118, 0.4392,  // es_pinksplash_08\n  0, 0.1569, 0.7804, 0.7725, 0.1961, 0.0392, 0.5961, 0.6078, 0.3765, 0.0039, 0.4353, 0.4706, 0.3765, 0.1686, 0.498, 0.6353, 0.5451, 0.0392, 0.2863, 0.4353, 1, 0.0039, 0.1333, 0.2784,  // Coral_reef\n  0, 0.3922, 0.6118, 0.6, 0.2, 0.0039, 0.3882, 0.5373, 0.3961, 0.0039, 0.2667, 0.3294, 0.4078, 0.1373, 0.5569, 0.6588, 0.698, 0, 0.2471, 0.4588, 1, 0.0039, 0.0392, 0.0392,  // es_ocean_breeze_068\n  0, 0.898, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0.2392, 0.949, 0.0157, 0.2471, 0.3961, 1, 0.0471, 1, 0.498, 0.9765, 0.3176, 0.9882, 0.6, 1, 0.0431, 0.9216, 0.7569, 0.9569, 0.0196, 0.2667, 1, 0.9098, 0.0039, 0.0196,  // es_pinksplash_07\n  0, 0.0157, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0.2, 0.0627, 0, 0.0039, 0.298, 0.3804, 0.4078, 0.0118, 0.3961, 1, 0.5137, 0.0745, 0.498, 0.2627, 0.0353, 0.0157, 0.6, 0.0627, 0, 0.0039, 0.898, 0.0157, 0.0039, 0.0039, 1, 0.0157, 0.0039, 0.0039,  // es_vintage_01\n  0, 0.0314, 0.0118, 0, 0.1647, 0.0902, 0.0275, 0, 0.2471, 0.2941, 0.149, 0.0235, 0.3294, 0.6627, 0.3882, 0.149, 0.4157, 0.8353, 0.6627, 0.4667, 0.4549, 1, 1, 1, 0.5412, 0.5294, 1, 0.5412, 0.5804, 0.0863, 1, 0.0941, 0.6667, 0, 1, 0, 0.749, 0, 0.5333, 0, 0.8314, 0, 0.2157, 0, 1, 0, 0.2157, 0,  // departure\n  0, 0, 0, 0, 0.1451, 0.0078, 0.098, 0.0039, 0.298, 0.0588, 0.451, 0.0196, 0.498, 0.3098, 0.8353, 0.0039, 0.502, 0.4941, 0.8275, 0.1843, 0.5098, 0.7373, 0.8196, 0.9686, 0.6, 0.5647, 0.7137, 0.8039, 0.8, 0.2314, 0.4588, 0.9804, 1, 0.0039, 0.1451, 0.7529,  // es_landscape_64\n  0, 0.0039, 0.0196, 0, 0.0745, 0.1255, 0.0902, 0.0039, 0.149, 0.6314, 0.2157, 0.0039, 0.2471, 0.898, 0.5647, 0.0039, 0.2588, 0.1529, 0.5569, 0.2902, 1, 0.0039, 0.0157, 0.0039,  // es_landscape_33\n  0, 1, 0.1294, 0.0157, 0.1686, 1, 0.2667, 0.098, 0.3373, 1, 0.0275, 0.098, 0.498, 1, 0.3216, 0.4039, 0.6667, 1, 1, 0.949, 0.8196, 0.1647, 1, 0.0863, 1, 0.3412, 1, 0.2549,  // rainbowsherbet\n  0, 0.9686, 0.6902, 0.9686, 0.1882, 1, 0.5333, 1, 0.349, 0.8627, 0.1137, 0.8863, 0.6275, 0.0275, 0.3216, 0.698, 0.8471, 0.0039, 0.4863, 0.4275, 1, 0.0039, 0.4863, 0.4275,  // gr65_hult\n  0, 0.0039, 0.4863, 0.4275, 0.2588, 0.0039, 0.3647, 0.3098, 0.4078, 0.2039, 0.2549, 0.0039, 0.5098, 0.451, 0.498, 0.0039, 0.5882, 0.2039, 0.2549, 0.0039, 0.7882, 0.0039, 0.3373, 0.2824, 0.9373, 0, 0.2157, 0.1765, 1, 0, 0.2157, 0.1765,  // gr64_hult\n  0, 0.1843, 0.1176, 0.0078, 0.1647, 0.8353, 0.5765, 0.0941, 0.3294, 0.4039, 0.8588, 0.2039, 0.498, 0.0118, 0.8588, 0.8118, 0.6667, 0.0039, 0.1882, 0.8392, 0.8314, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0.4353, 1, 0.0039, 0.0275, 0.1294,  // GMT_drywet\n  0, 0.7608, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0.3686, 0.0039, 0.1137, 0.0706, 0.5176, 0.2235, 0.5137, 0.1098, 1, 0.4431, 0.0039, 0.0039,  // ib_jul01\n  0, 0.0078, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0.2078, 0.0706, 0.0039, 0, 0.4078, 0.2706, 0.1137, 0.0039, 0.6, 0.6549, 0.5294, 0.0392, 1, 0.1804, 0.2196, 0.0157,  // es_vintage_57\n  0, 0.4431, 0.3569, 0.5765, 0.2824, 0.6157, 0.3451, 0.3059, 0.349, 0.8157, 0.3333, 0.1294, 0.4196, 1, 0.1137, 0.0431, 0.5529, 0.5373, 0.1216, 0.1529, 1, 0.2314, 0.1294, 0.349,  // ib15\n  0, 0.1686, 0.0118, 0.6, 0.2471, 0.3922, 0.0157, 0.4039, 0.498, 0.7373, 0.0196, 0.2588, 0.749, 0.6314, 0.0431, 0.451, 1, 0.5294, 0.0784, 0.7137,  // Fuschia_7\n  0, 0.3804, 1, 0.0039, 0.3961, 0.1843, 0.5216, 0.0039, 0.698, 0.051, 0.1686, 0.0039, 1, 0.0078, 0.0392, 0.0039,  // es_emerald_dragon_08\n  0, 0, 0, 0, 0.1804, 0.0706, 0, 0, 0.3765, 0.4431, 0, 0, 0.4235, 0.5569, 0.0118, 0.0039, 0.4667, 0.6863, 0.0667, 0.0039, 0.5725, 0.8353, 0.1725, 0.0078, 0.6824, 1, 0.3216, 0.0157, 0.7373, 1, 0.451, 0.0157, 0.7922, 1, 0.6118, 0.0157, 0.8549, 1, 0.7961, 0.0157, 0.9176, 1, 1, 0.0157, 0.9569, 1, 1, 0.2784, 1, 1, 1, 1,  // lava\n  0, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0, 0.298, 0.1255, 0.0196, 0, 0.5725, 0.7529, 0.0941, 0, 0.7725, 0.8627, 0.4118, 0.0196, 0.9412, 0.9882, 1, 0.1216, 0.9804, 0.9882, 1, 0.4353, 1, 1, 1, 1,  // fire\n  0, 0.0392, 0.3333, 0.0196, 0.098, 0.1137, 0.4275, 0.0706, 0.2353, 0.2314, 0.5412, 0.1647, 0.3647, 0.3255, 0.3882, 0.2039, 0.4157, 0.4314, 0.2588, 0.251, 0.4275, 0.4824, 0.1922, 0.2549, 0.4431, 0.5451, 0.1373, 0.2588, 0.4549, 0.7529, 0.4588, 0.3843, 0.4863, 1, 1, 0.5373, 0.6588, 0.3922, 0.7059, 0.6078, 1, 0.0863, 0.4745, 0.6824,  // Colorfull\n  0, 0.2784, 0.1059, 0.1529, 0.1216, 0.5098, 0.0431, 0.2, 0.2471, 0.8353, 0.0078, 0.251, 0.2745, 0.9098, 0.0039, 0.2588, 0.298, 0.9882, 0.0039, 0.2706, 0.4235, 0.4824, 0.0078, 0.2, 1, 0.1804, 0.0353, 0.1373,  // Magenta_Evening\n  0, 0.0745, 0.0078, 0.1529, 0.098, 0.102, 0.0157, 0.1765, 0.2, 0.1294, 0.0235, 0.2039, 0.298, 0.2667, 0.2431, 0.4902, 0.4, 0.4627, 0.7333, 0.9412, 0.4275, 0.6392, 0.8431, 0.9686, 0.4471, 0.851, 0.9569, 1, 0.4784, 0.6235, 0.5843, 0.8667, 0.5843, 0.4431, 0.3059, 0.7373, 0.7176, 0.502, 0.2235, 0.6078, 1, 0.5725, 0.1569, 0.4824,  // Pink_Purple\n  0, 0.102, 0.0039, 0.0039, 0.2, 0.2627, 0.0157, 0.0039, 0.3294, 0.4627, 0.0549, 0.0039, 0.4078, 0.5373, 0.5961, 0.2039, 0.4392, 0.4431, 0.2549, 0.0039, 0.4784, 0.5216, 0.5843, 0.2314, 0.4863, 0.5373, 0.5961, 0.2039, 0.5294, 0.4431, 0.2549, 0.0039, 0.5569, 0.5451, 0.6039, 0.1804, 0.6392, 0.4431, 0.051, 0.0039, 0.8, 0.2157, 0.0118, 0.0039, 0.9765, 0.0667, 0.0039, 0.0039, 1, 0.0667, 0.0039, 0.0039,  // es_autumn_19\n  0, 0, 0, 0, 0.1647, 0, 0, 0.1765, 0.3294, 0, 0, 1, 0.498, 0.1647, 0, 1, 0.6667, 1, 0, 1, 0.8314, 1, 0.2157, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1,  // BlacK_Blue_Magenta_White\n  0, 0, 0, 0, 0.2471, 0.1647, 0, 0.1765, 0.498, 1, 0, 1, 0.749, 1, 0, 0.1765, 1, 1, 0, 0,  // BlacK_Magenta_Red\n  0, 0, 0, 0, 0.1647, 0.1647, 0, 0, 0.3294, 1, 0, 0, 0.498, 1, 0, 0.1765, 0.6667, 1, 0, 1, 0.8314, 1, 0.2157, 0.1765, 1, 1, 1, 0,  // BlacK_Red_Magenta_Yellow\n  0, 0, 0, 1, 0.2471, 0, 0.2157, 1, 0.498, 0, 1, 1, 0.749, 0.1647, 1, 0.1765, 1, 1, 1, 0,  // Blue_Cyan_Yellow\n  0, 0.0118, 0.0078, 0.0941, 0.1176, 0.1569, 0.0784, 0.5098, 0.2275, 0.3608, 0.1765, 1, 0.3451, 0.7451, 0, 0.7059, 0.4627, 1, 0.1255, 0.2824, 0.6039, 1, 0.3725, 0, 0.7686, 1, 0.5882, 0, 0.8863, 1, 0.2824, 0, 1, 0.0941, 0.0039, 0.0706,  // K1_Iris_Apricot\n  0, 0, 0.0157, 0.0706, 0.1098, 0, 0.1647, 0.2745, 0.2275, 0, 0.5882, 0.6275, 0.3451, 0, 0.8627, 0.8235, 0.4549, 0.3216, 0.8627, 0, 0.5647, 0.1333, 0.5882, 0, 0.6667, 0, 0.2157, 0.0392, 0.7451, 0.0314, 0.0118, 0.0706, 0.8471, 0.6471, 0, 0.5098, 0.9333, 0.9608, 0, 0.6667, 1, 0.0471, 0.0078, 0.1098,  // K1_Tropical_Ultraviolet\n  0, 0, 0.0196, 0.1373, 0.1255, 0, 0.3529, 0.5686, 0.2588, 0, 0.8235, 0.902, 0.3843, 0, 0.5098, 0.6275, 0.4941, 0.4706, 0, 1, 0.6039, 0.7059, 0, 1, 0.7137, 0.9216, 0, 0.6863, 0.8314, 1, 0.5098, 0, 0.9255, 1, 0.3333, 0, 1, 0, 0.0196, 0.1373,  // K1_Chameleon_Flare\n  0, 0.0706, 0, 0.0118, 0.1333, 0.3765, 0.0314, 0.0392, 0.2745, 0.8235, 0.1373, 0.1569, 0.4118, 1, 0.2824, 0.1765, 0.5412, 1, 0.4118, 0.0784, 0.6745, 1, 0.5882, 0, 0.8039, 1, 0.7451, 0.0784, 0.9098, 0.6667, 0, 0.3725, 1, 0.0706, 0, 0.0118,  // K1_Coral_Sunset\n  0, 0, 0.0118, 0.0706, 0.1333, 0, 0.0784, 0.3529, 0.2667, 0, 0.3333, 0.7451, 0.4, 0, 0.7059, 0.8627, 0.5176, 0, 0.4314, 0.5098, 0.6275, 0, 0.0784, 0.1569, 0.7137, 0.0157, 0.0078, 0.0392, 0.8157, 1, 0.5294, 0, 0.9176, 1, 0.2941, 0, 1, 0.1373, 0, 0.0314,  // K1_Night_Sea_Amber\n  0, 0.0471, 0, 0.0392, 0.1255, 0.2549, 0, 0.1765, 0.251, 0.5686, 0, 0.3137, 0.3765, 0.8627, 0, 0.2745, 0.502, 1, 0.1412, 0.0941, 0.6275, 1, 0.3608, 0, 0.7529, 1, 0.5686, 0, 0.8549, 1, 0.7451, 0.1569, 0.9412, 1, 0.2745, 0.4706, 1, 0.0471, 0, 0.0392,  // K1_Crimson_Gold\n  0, 0.0314, 0, 0.0941, 0.1333, 0.1176, 0, 0.5098, 0.2745, 0.2745, 0, 0.9216, 0.4078, 0.5098, 0, 1, 0.5412, 0.7451, 0, 0.8627, 0.6745, 0.9216, 0, 0.6275, 0.8078, 1, 0.0314, 0.3765, 0.9098, 1, 0, 0.2353, 1, 0.0314, 0, 0.0941,  // K1_Ultraviolet_Ascend\n  0, 0.0078, 0, 0.0784, 0.1333, 0.0392, 0, 0.549, 0.2745, 0.1098, 0, 0.8824, 0.4157, 0.2745, 0.0392, 1, 0.549, 0.4706, 0, 1, 0.6667, 0.1569, 0, 0.4706, 0.7451, 0.0235, 0.0078, 0.0549, 0.8314, 1, 0.549, 0, 0.9255, 1, 0.3725, 0, 1, 0.0078, 0, 0.0784,  // K1_Naberius_Gold\n  0, 0.0549, 0, 0.0549, 0.149, 0.251, 0, 0.1882, 0.3059, 0.5882, 0, 0.3137, 0.4549, 0.8627, 0, 0.4706, 0.5961, 1, 0, 0.5882, 0.7373, 1, 0.1176, 0.4706, 0.8627, 1, 0.2745, 0.5882, 1, 0.0549, 0, 0.0549,  // K1_Vepar_Pink\n  0, 0, 0.0627, 0.0235, 0.1333, 0, 0.6667, 0.1569, 0.2588, 0, 0.8627, 0.4706, 0.3843, 0, 0.8235, 0.8235, 0.5098, 0, 0.4706, 1, 0.6353, 0.2353, 0.1176, 1, 0.7608, 0.549, 0, 1, 0.8784, 0.8627, 0, 0.6667, 1, 0.0627, 0, 0.0549,  // K1_Flourish_Sweep\n  0, 1, 0.0314, 0.3765, 0.2039, 0.9216, 0, 0.6275, 0.4078, 0.7451, 0, 0.8627, 0.6118, 0.5098, 0, 1, 0.8157, 0.2745, 0, 0.9216, 1, 0.1176, 0, 0.5098  // K1_Ultraviolet_Bright\n]\n// Exact RGB stop-walk sample of K1 palette idx at position t (writes pr/pg/pb).\n// K1 palette bytes are already gamma-converted for WS2812B -- pass to rgb() as-is,\n// do NOT re-gamma.\nvar pr, pg, pb\nfunction palSample(idx, t) {\n  var o = palOff[idx]\n  var n = palLen[idx]\n  t = mod(t, 1)\n  var base = o * 4\n  var i\n  for (i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n    if (t < palData[base + (i + 1) * 4]) break\n  }\n  if (i >= n - 1) i = n - 2\n  var i0 = base + i * 4\n  var i1 = i0 + 4\n  var p0 = palData[i0], p1 = palData[i1]\n  var f = p1 > p0 ? (t - p0) / (p1 - p0) : 0\n  pr = mix(palData[i0 + 1], palData[i1 + 1], f)\n  pg = mix(palData[i0 + 2], palData[i1 + 2], f)\n  pb = mix(palData[i0 + 3], palData[i1 + 3], f)\n}\n// Unified mode evaluation: 0..14 = HSV demos, 15..58 = K1 bank. Writes or/og/ob.\nvar MODE_COUNT = numHsvModes + PAL_COUNT   // 59\nfunction evalMode(m, hh, pct) {\n  if (m < numHsvModes) {\n    modes[m](hh, pct)\n  } else {\n    palSample(m - numHsvModes, hh)\n    or = pr; og = pg; ob = pb\n  }\n}\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Transition engine: every mode/palette switch crossfades, never cuts.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------\nvar curMode = 0, prevMode = 0\nvar blend = 1, blendF = 1       // fade progress / smoothstepped mix\nvar dwellT = 0\nvar booted = 0\nvar dwell = 6\nexport function sliderDwellTime(v) { dwell = 1 + 29 * v }        // 1..30s per palette\nvar fadeTime = 1.5\nexport function sliderFadeTime(v) { fadeTime = 0.1 + 4.9 * v }   // 0.1..5s crossfade\nvar autoCycle = 1\nexport function toggleAutoCycle(v) { autoCycle = v }\nvar k1Only = 1\nexport function toggleK1Only(v) { k1Only = v }                   // auto-cycle skips HSV demos\nvar pendingMode = -1\nexport function sliderModeSelect(v) {\n  var m = min(MODE_COUNT - 1, floor(v * MODE_COUNT))\n  if (!booted) { switchTo(m); return }   // pattern-load restore: instant, no fade\n  if (m != curMode) pendingMode = m      // queued; applied when current fade completes\n}\nexport function showNumberMode() { return curMode }\nexport function showNumberK1Palette() { return curMode >= numHsvModes ? curMode - numHsvModes : -1 }\nfunction switchTo(m) {\n  prevMode = curMode\n  curMode = m\n  blend = booted ? 0 : 1        // pattern-load restore: no boot fade\n}\nfunction nextMode() {\n  var n = curMode + 1\n  if (n >= MODE_COUNT) n = k1Only ? numHsvModes : 0\n  if (k1Only && n < numHsvModes) n = numHsvModes\n  return n\n}\nexport function beforeRender(delta) {\n  var dt = delta / 1000\n  if (dt > 0.1) dt = 0.1\n  booted = 1\n  t1 = time(10 / 65.535)        // Animate hue's phase angle (original behaviour)\n  if (autoCycle) {\n    dwellT += dt\n    if (dwellT >= dwell) { dwellT = 0; pendingMode = nextMode() }\n  }\n  // switches only fire when settled -> a mid-fade retarget is impossible by\n  // construction, so the crossfade can never produce a discontinuity\n  if (blend >= 1 && pendingMode >= 0 && pendingMode != curMode) {\n    switchTo(pendingMode)\n    pendingMode = -1\n    dwellT = 0\n  }\n  if (blend < 1) {\n    var ft = min(fadeTime, dwell * 0.9)   // fade always completes within a dwell\n    blend = min(1, blend + dt / ft)\n  }\n  blendF = blend * blend * (3 - 2 * blend)  // smoothstep ease\n}\n// Simple linear chase (original), now with dual-eval crossfade on transitions\nexport function render(index) {\n  var pct = index / pixelCount\n  var hh = (1 + pct - t1) % 1 // Remove t1 to stop animation and inspect a palette\n  evalMode(curMode, hh, pct)\n  if (blendF < 1) {\n    var r2 = or, g2 = og, b2 = ob        // incoming mode\n    evalMode(prevMode, hh, pct)          // outgoing mode -> or/og/ob\n    var f = blendF\n    rgb(or + (r2 - or) * f, og + (g2 - og) * f, ob + (b2 - ob) * f)\n  } else {\n    rgb(or, og, ob)\n  }\n}\n// Posterize - lookup discreet outputs for continuous 0...1 inputs\nfunction posterize(h, palette) { return remap(h, palette, 0) }\n// Hue traverse - remap 0...1 to 0...1 with interpolation, picking the \n// shortest path around the hue wheel, including wrapping from 1 to 0.\nfunction hFn(h, palette) { return remap(h, palette, 1) }\n// Interpolate - remap 0...1 to 0...1 interpolating between specified points\nfunction unitFn(x, palette) { return remap(x, palette, 2) }\n// Color grade: Remap a 0...1 input through palettes to all three of h, s, & v\nfunction grade(input, hsv_palette) {\n  h =    hFn(input, hsv_palette[0])\n  s = unitFn(input, hsv_palette[1])\n  v = unitFn(input, hsv_palette[2])\n  outHsv(h, s, v)\n}\n/* Given x in 0...1 (typically a hue but can be used with saturation or value)\n   and a remapping array (usually a color palette) of size paletteSize\n   remap x through the palette to other 0...1 y values. \n   mode sets the interpolation style.\n   mode = 0: Posterize by looking up a single value for each input region.\n   mode = 1: Continuously (linearly) interpolate using the shortest path (-0.5..0.5)\n     around a hue color wheel to produce a gradient between hues.\n   mode = 2: Interpolate between values without wrapping 1 -> 0. Useful for s or v.\n*/\nfunction remap(x, palette, mode) {\n  x = (x + 255) % 1 // Wrap hue inputs like hsv() does\n  w1 = palette[0]\n  firstPosition = floor(palette[0])\n  firstY = palette[0] % 1\n  lastPosition = floor(palette[paletteSize - 1])\n  lastY = palette[paletteSize - 1] % 1\n  inputPosition = x * 999\n  \n  // inputPosition is less than the first 0-999 position or greater than the final one\n  if (inputPosition < firstPosition || inputPosition > lastPosition) {\n    if (mode == 0) { return lastY }\n    sectionPositionDistance = 999 - (lastPosition - firstPosition)\n    if (sectionPositionDistance <= 0) { return lastY }    // K1 fix: same guard for the wrap section\n    dY = yDistance(lastY, firstY, mode)\n    sectionPct = (((1000 + inputPosition - lastPosition) %  1000) / sectionPositionDistance) % 1\n    return (lastY + sectionPct * dY) % 1\n  }\n  \n  // inputPosition is within the positions specified in the palette\n  for (i = 0;  i < paletteSize - 1; i++) {\n    thisPosition = floor(palette[i])\n    nextPosition = floor(palette[i+1])\n    if (thisPosition <= inputPosition && inputPosition <= nextPosition ) {\n      thisY = palette[i] % 1\n      if (mode == 0) { return thisY }\n      sectionPositionDistance = nextPosition - thisPosition\n      if (sectionPositionDistance <= 0) { return thisY }  // K1 fix: duplicate positions -> div/0 -> NaN in original\n      dY = yDistance(thisY, palette[i+1] % 1, mode)\n      sectionPct = (inputPosition - thisPosition)/sectionPositionDistance\n      return (thisY + sectionPct * dY) % 1\n    }\n  }\n}\n/* \n  mode = 0: no-op. Unexpected. Could return 0.\n  mode = 1:\n     Takes two hues, 0...1, and calculates the shortest signed distance \n     from h1 to h2, which will in -0.5..0.5.\n     If h2 > h1 by <0.5, or h1 > h2 by >0.5, the shortest route around \n     the wheel is the positive direction.\n  mode = 2:\n     Signed distance without wrapping from 1 to 0. Useful for s & v maps\n*/\nfunction yDistance(y1, y2, mode) {  \n  distance = y2 - y1\n  if (mode == 2 || abs(distance) < 0.5) return distance\n  if (y2 > y1) return distance - 1\n  return distance + 1\n}\n"}, "preview": ""}